Enables/disables directional slope shading

SYNOPSIS

    h.set_sun(True, sun_az_deg = 135, sun_el_deg = 45)

DESCRIPTION

Mirrors horizonator_set_sun() in horizonator.h. When shading_enabled is
False (the default), rendering is unchanged (the plain distance-based
grayscale/materials coloring, with no directional lighting). sun_az_deg
(0=North, 90=East) and sun_el_deg (0=horizon, 90=straight up) give the
direction TOWARDS the sun; both are ignored when shading_enabled is
False.

ARGUMENTS

- shading_enabled: boolean

- sun_az_deg: optional float, defaulting to 135 (southeast)

- sun_el_deg: optional float, defaulting to 45

RETURNED VALUES

None. Raises an exception on failure.
